# LeetCode 15 - 3Sum

## Problem
Brief description.

## Approach
Explain the algorithm in 4–6 points.

## Algorithm
1. Sort the array.
2. Fix one element.
3. Use two pointers.
4. Skip duplicates.
5. Store valid triplets.

## Time Complexity
O(n²)

## Space Complexity
O(1)

## Concepts Used
- Arrays
- Sorting
- Two Pointers

//code
class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> threeSum(int[] nums) {

        // List to store all unique triplets
        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();

        // Sort the array to use the two-pointer approach
        Arrays.sort(nums);

        int n = nums.length;

        // Fix the first element of the triplet
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {

            // Skip duplicate first elements to avoid duplicate triplets
            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) {
                continue;
            }

            // Two pointers
            int left = i + 1;
            int right = n - 1;

            while (left < right) {

                int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];

                if (sum == 0) {

                    // Valid triplet found
                    res.add(Arrays.asList(nums[i], nums[left], nums[right]));

                    // Skip duplicate values on the left
                    while (left < right && nums[left] == nums[left + 1]) {
                        left++;
                    }

                    // Skip duplicate values on the right
                    while (left < right && nums[right] == nums[right - 1]) {
                        right--;
                    }

                    // Move both pointers to search for another pair
                    left++;
                    right--;
                }

                // Sum is too large, decrease it
                else if (sum > 0) {
                    right--;
                }

                // Sum is too small, increase it
                else {
                    left++;
                }
            }
        }

        // Return all unique triplets
        return res;
    }
}
